Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.00,0:00:01.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}1945.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.40,0:00:04.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Manila, in the Philippines. A U.S.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.13,0:00:08.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Army film crew records a patient being moved out of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.23,0:00:09.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}a military hospital.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:01.25,0:00:07.00,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1038 0 l 1038 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:01.25,0:00:07.00,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:01.25,0:00:07.00,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}"IRON LUNG EVACUATION" · 60TH GENERAL HOSPITAL, MANILA
Dialogue: 3,0:00:01.25,0:00:07.00,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1945 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.28,0:00:12.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The patient isn't on a stretcher.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.16,0:00:13.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The patient is inside a machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.99,0:00:15.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}A steel tank, loaded onto a plane.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.37,0:00:18.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It was called an iron lung.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.13,0:00:19.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And it did one job.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.37,0:00:21.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It breathed for people who could not.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.48,0:00:26.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}For decades, the disease that filled these machines
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.12,0:00:27.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}came back every summer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.77,0:00:30.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It was called infantile paralysis. Polio.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:22.73,0:00:28.48,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1208 0 l 1208 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:22.73,0:00:28.48,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:22.73,0:00:28.48,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}"UNCONDITIONAL SURRENDER" · NATIONAL FOUNDATION FOR INFANTILE PARALYSIS
Dialogue: 3,0:00:22.73,0:00:28.48,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1956
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.14,0:00:35.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Then, in about 25 years, America stopped wild polio
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.05,0:00:37.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}from spreading. This is how.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.00,0:00:46.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Polio is caused by a virus.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.57,0:00:49.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}According to the World Health Organization, it
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.25,0:00:52.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}spreads mainly from person to person, through what's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.28,0:00:53.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}called the fecal-oral route.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:45.25,0:00:51.00,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 757 0 l 757 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:45.25,0:00:51.00,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:00:45.25,0:00:51.00,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}NATIONAL FOUNDATION FOR INFANTILE PARALYSIS
Dialogue: 3,0:00:45.25,0:00:51.00,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1956
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.38,0:01:14.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And when the paralysis reached the muscles used for
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.45,0:01:17.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}breathing, 5 to 10 percent of those paralyzed died.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.08,0:01:38.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In the late 1940s and early fifties, according to
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.34,0:01:42.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the CDC, polio crippled an average of more than
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.43,0:01:45.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}35,000 people a year in the U.S.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.30,0:03:14.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Iron lungs were meant to give temporary relief,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.93,0:03:16.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}until a patient recovered.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.94,0:03:18.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}But not everyone did.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.56,0:03:22.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In 1959, about 1,200 people in the United States
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.26,0:03:24.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}were still using tank respirators.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:11.55,0:03:17.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1038 0 l 1038 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:03:11.55,0:03:17.30,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:03:11.55,0:03:17.30,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}IRON LUNG EVACUATION · MANILA
Dialogue: 3,0:03:11.55,0:03:17.30,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1945 · U.S. ARMY SIGNAL CORPS
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.98,0:03:47.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In August 1921, at 39, Franklin D.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.53,0:03:51.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Roosevelt was diagnosed with infantile paralysis.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.20,0:03:54.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In 1924, he went to Warm Springs, Georgia, hoping
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.87,0:03:56.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}its waters would help.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.52,0:03:59.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Two years later, he bought the resort.
Dialogue: 2,0:03:45.23,0:03:50.98,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1038 0 l 1038 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:03:45.23,0:03:50.98,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:03:45.23,0:03:50.98,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}FDR PRESIDENTIAL LIBRARY
Dialogue: 3,0:03:45.23,0:03:50.98,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · WARM SPRINGS, GA. · 1928–1939
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.73,0:04:22.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Movie audiences gave.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.22,0:04:25.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In this nineteen 44 newsreel, a young girl on
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.41,0:04:28.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}crutches thanks moviegoers for their dimes.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:20.98,0:04:26.73,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 802 0 l 802 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:04:20.98,0:04:26.73,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:04:20.98,0:04:26.73,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}"THANKS FOR THE DIMES"
Dialogue: 3,0:04:20.98,0:04:26.73,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}UNIVERSAL NEWSREEL · FEB. 28, 1944
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.91,0:04:31.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And the National Foundation would pick the man to
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.01,0:04:34.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}run what PBS NewsHour calls the largest vaccine
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.98,0:04:36.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}trial of its kind ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.57,0:04:43.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In the early 1950s, Salk developed an inactivated
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.25,0:04:44.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}polio vaccine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.31,0:04:45.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}It used killed virus.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.89,0:04:49.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In this 1956 film, made by the National Foundation,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.72,0:04:53.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the vaccine is produced and checked, batch by batch.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:39.82,0:04:45.57,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 886 0 l 886 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:04:39.82,0:04:45.57,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:04:39.82,0:04:45.57,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}POLIO VACCINE PRODUCTION · NATIONAL FOUNDATION FILM
Dialogue: 3,0:04:39.82,0:04:45.57,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1956
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.09,0:04:57.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}To find out if it worked, the National Foundation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.13,0:05:00.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}turned to Salk's former teacher, Thomas Francis Jr.,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.37,0:05:02.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}at the University of Michigan.
Dialogue: 2,0:04:54.34,0:05:00.09,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 676 0 l 676 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:04:54.34,0:05:00.09,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:04:54.34,0:05:00.09,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}VACCINE LAB · NATIONAL FOUNDATION FILM
Dialogue: 3,0:04:54.34,0:05:00.09,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1956
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.42,0:05:20.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In part of the trial, some children got the vaccine,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.52,0:05:23.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}and a group at least as large got a placebo.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.14,0:05:24.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}That part was double-blind.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.75,0:05:27.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Neither the children nor the doctors giving the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.55,0:05:29.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}shots knew which was which.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:17.67,0:05:23.42,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 757 0 l 757 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:17.67,0:05:23.42,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:17.67,0:05:23.42,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}NATIONAL FOUNDATION FOR INFANTILE PARALYSIS
Dialogue: 3,0:05:17.67,0:05:23.42,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1956
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.50,0:05:54.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}That same year, 1955, the vaccine was licensed for
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.28,0:05:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}use in the United States.
Dialogue: 2,0:05:50.75,0:05:56.50,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 502 0 l 502 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:50.75,0:05:56.50,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:05:50.75,0:05:56.50,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}POLIOMYELITIS VACCINE VIALS
Dialogue: 3,0:05:50.75,0:05:56.50,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1956
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.81,0:06:33.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Vaccination went on.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.31,0:06:37.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In this 1957 newsreel, the Salk vaccine is given to
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.16,0:06:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}children, including twin girls.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:32.06,0:06:37.81,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 738 0 l 738 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:32.06,0:06:37.81,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:32.06,0:06:37.81,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}SALK VACCINE BEING GIVEN
Dialogue: 3,0:06:32.06,0:06:37.81,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}UNIVERSAL NEWSREEL · APRIL 1957
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.68,0:06:46.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In 1961, the Communicable Disease Center, today's
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.16,0:06:49.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}CDC, filmed a polio vaccination campaign in
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.21,0:06:52.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Columbus, Georgia, with the state and county health
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.83,0:06:53.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}departments.
Dialogue: 2,0:06:42.93,0:06:48.68,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1146 0 l 1146 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:42.93,0:06:48.68,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H00A3B32B\1a&H00&\p1}m 0 0 l 10 0 l 10 132 l 0 132{\p0}
Dialogue: 3,0:06:42.93,0:06:48.68,Kick,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,846,126,846,0,350)\fad(250,300)}"BABIES AND BREADWINNERS" · COLUMBUS, GA.
Dialogue: 3,0:06:42.93,0:06:48.68,Head,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(106,878,126,878,0,350)\fad(250,300)}ARCHIVAL FILM · 1961 · COMMUNICABLE DISEASE CENTER
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.13,0:06:55.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Free vaccine stations went up.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.92,0:06:58.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Signs went up on street corners and buses.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.42,0:06:59.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The message was simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.79,0:07:00.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}One shot, good.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.69,0:07:01.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Two shots, better.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.76,0:07:02.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Three shots, best.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.28,0:07:05.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Health workers went door to door with forms.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.89,0:07:08.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}And the campaign kept score, charting how many young
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.98,0:07:11.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}children in each area had three or more shots.
Dialogue: 2,0:07:03.53,0:07:09.28,Box,,0,0,0,,{\an7\move(76,828,96,828,0,350)\fad(250,300)\bord0\shad0\1c&H0014120A\1a&H30&\p1}m 0 0 l 1146 0 l 1146 132 l 0 132{\p0}
